# Final review — etude-aul.4

## Outcome

The existing `etude bench` leaf now has an explicit, mutually exclusive gate
mode. It accepts `--gate`, repeated `--variant`, `--cohort run-refs`, and
optional strict `--labels`; evaluates every variant/fixture cell through the
landed gate evaluator; scores every variant over one common successful fixture
set; and renders aggregate provenance plus every successful or failed cell.

## Decision

Extend the existing leaf rather than introduce `bench gate`. The existing
`internal/cli/bench.go` owns cohort limits, judge resolution, timeout plumbing,
dependency seams, and report rendering. Converting the shipped `bench <stage>`
leaf into a command group would require a compatibility shim or break its public
syntax. Conditional argument validation and explicit cross-mode flag rejection
make the two behaviors unambiguous without duplicating that machinery.

## Scope

Only the three authorized aul.4 paths changed:

- `internal/cli/bench.go`
- `internal/cli/bench_test.go`
- `docs/bench.md`

The generated `docs/cli/etude_bench.md` is intentionally the immediately
following `etude-aul.5` commit. The two commits will be pushed together; the
temporary generated-doc drift is not a terminal or remote state.

